{"text": "PHILIP MORRIS\nU.S.A.\n\nP. 0. Box 26603, RICHMOND, VIRGINIA 23261\nDecember 6, 1999\n\nTo: \u2014 G.R. Schmidt\n\nZa Wiw\u2014\u2014\n\nFrom:\n\n. Newmnal\n\nSubject: Mentholated Foil Equilibration and Release Procedures\n\nAll menthol products manufactured utilizing mentholated foil must be equilibrated for ten (10)\ndays, from the date of manufacture, in either cold or dry storage.\n\nMentholated foil products can be transported among Philip Morris controlled facilities during the\nten (10) day equilibration period.\n\nMentholated foil products can be designated as released from equilibration hold on finished goods\ninventory control systems at the end of the ninth (9\") day in order that they can be recognized as\neligible for shipment on the 10\" day. However, no mentholated foil products will be shipped from\nPhilip Morris controlled facilities prior to the 11\" day after their manufacture.\n\nTo optimize product freshness, it is recommended that mentholated foil product be kept in cold\nstorage as long as practically possible. Dry storage should be utilized to equilibrate and/or store\nmentholated foil product that is needed to fill orders scheduled to ship within the near future.\n\n\u2018Mentholated foil product placed in cold storage must be tempered following the appropriate\ntempering guidelines.\n\n* This procedure supersedes all other procedures, guidelines, or requirements issued\nregarding mentholated foil product handling, and will be in effect until superseded.\n\n{RNC DFU SVRINEWMANKACCONDM DESIGN Data FOSZeno!- Geer el Fle 1-169 doe\n\noeezigezoz", "words": [{"text": "PHILIP", "x0": 237, "y0": 190, "x1": 356, "y1": 210, "conf": 95.0}, {"text": "MORRIS", "x0": 372, "y0": 190, "x1": 512, "y1": 210, "conf": 96.0}, {"text": "U.S.A.", "x0": 346, "y0": 221, "x1": 406, "y1": 236, "conf": 87.0}, {"text": "P.", "x0": 233, "y0": 262, "x1": 241, "y1": 272, "conf": 80.0}, {"text": "0.", "x0": 248, "y0": 262, "x1": 261, "y1": 272, "conf": 40.0}, {"t